1e:T468,Authority assigned to a State officer- (a) is a public trust to be exercised in a manner that- (i) is consistent with the purposes and objects of this Constitution; (ii) demonstrates respect for the people; (iii) brings honour to the nation and dignity to the office; and (iv) promotes public confidence in the integrity of the office; and (b) vests in the State officer the responsibility to serve the people, rather than the power to rule them.

The guiding principles of leadership and integrity include- (a) selection on the basis of personal integrity, competence and suitability, or election in free and fair elections; (b) objectivity and impartiality in decision making, and in ensuring that decisions are not influenced by nepotism, favouritism, other improper motives or corrupt practices; (c) selfless service based solely on the public interest, demonstrated by (i) honesty in the execution of public duties; and (ii) the declaration of any personal interest that may conflict with public duties; (d) accountability to the public for decisions and actions; and (e) discipline and commitment in service to the people.10:["$","main",null,{"className":"flex-1 max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 lg:px-12 py-10 sm:py-14 w-full space-y-12","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-white border border-rule rounded-card overflow-hidden","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"p-6 sm:p-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline justify-between gap-4 mb-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-sans font-black text-6xl sm:text-[72px] text-flag-green leading-none","children":6}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-sans text-xs font-bold text-ink px-2.5 py-1 border border-ink rounded-card","children":"Accountability"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"font-sans text-xs font-bold text-ink px-2.5 py-1 border border-ink rounded-card","children":"Articles 73 to 80"}]]}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-[clamp(32px,4.4vw,56px)] font-black text-ink tracking-[-0.03em] leading-[1.02] font-sans","children":"Leadership and Integrity"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-serif italic text-base sm:text-lg text-ink-muted mt-2","children":["Kiswahili: ","Uongozi na Maadili"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-serif text-[17px] sm:text-[19px] text-ink mt-4 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl","children":"Establishes that public office is a trust to be exercised with honor, dignity, and accountability to the people. Sets strict standards against conflicts of interest and corruption."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"background":"linear-gradient(to right, #111111 0% 30%, #be1111 30% 80%, #0a5c27 80% 100%)","height":"6px","width":"100%"},"className":"flex-shrink-0 ","aria-hidden":"true"}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"p-6 sm:p-8 bg-paper border border-rule border-l-[6px] border-l-flag-green rounded-card","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-sans font-bold text-base sm:text-lg text-ink mb-3","children":"Key constitutional takeaways"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"font-serif text-[17px] text-ink leading-relaxed flex items-start gap-2.5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-sans font-black text-flag-green text-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":"•"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Authority assigned to a State officer is a public trust."}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"font-serif text-[17px] text-ink leading-relaxed flex items-start gap-2.5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-sans font-black text-flag-green text-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":"•"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"State officers must avoid any conflict of interest between private gain and public duty."}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"font-serif text-[17px] text-ink leading-relaxed flex items-start gap-2.5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-sans font-black text-flag-green text-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":"•"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Financial probity, open declaration of foreign bank accounts, and civic accountability."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-[clamp(28px,3.6vw,44px)] font-black text-ink tracking-[-0.025em] leading-[1.05] font-sans","children":["Articles in Chapter ",6]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-serif text-ink-muted text-base mt-1","children":"Select an article to read its legal clauses and plain language meaning."}]]}],["$","$L1d",null,{"articles":[{"articleNumber":73,"title":"Responsibilities of leadership","summary":"Authority assigned to a State officer must be exercised in a manner that honors the nation and promotes public confidence.","content":"$1e","clauses":[{"clauseNumber":"(1)","text":"Authority assigned to a State officer- (a) is a public trust to be exercised in a manner that- (i) is consistent with the purposes and objects of this Constitution; (ii) demonstrates respect for the people; (iii) brings honour to the nation and dignity to the office; and (iv) promotes public confidence in the integrity of the office; and (b) vests in the State officer the responsibility to serve the people, rather than the power to rule them."},{"clauseNumber":"(2)","text":"The guiding principles of leadership and integrity include- (a) selection on the basis of personal integrity, competence and suitability, or election in free and fair elections; (b) objectivity and impartiality in decision making, and in ensuring that decisions are not influenced by nepotism, favouritism, other improper motives or corrupt practices; (c) selfless service based solely on the public interest, demonstrated by (i) honesty in the execution of public duties; and (ii) the declaration of any personal interest that may conflict with public duties; (d) accountability to the public for decisions and actions; and (e) discipline and commitment in service to the people."}],"plainExplanation":"Elected and appointed officials are public servants obligated to serve the people, not rulers above scrutiny."},{"articleNumber":74,"title":"Oath of office of State officers","content":"Before assuming a State office, acting in a State office, or performing any functions of a State office, a person shall take and subscribe the oath or affirmation of office, in the manner and form prescribed by the Third Schedule or under an Act of Parliament."},{"articleNumber":75,"title":"Conduct of State officers","summary":"Bars State officers from engaging in conflicts of interest, demeaning office dignity, or compromising public duties.","content":"A State officer shall behave, whether in public and official life, in private life, or in association with other persons, in a manner that avoids- (a) any conflict between personal interests and public or official duties; (b) compromising any public or official interest in favour of a personal interest; or (c) demeaning the office the officer holds.\n\nA person who contravenes clause (1), or Article 76, 77 or 78(2)- (a) shall be subject to the applicable disciplinary procedure for the relevant office; and (b) may, in accordance with the disciplinary procedure referred to in paragraph (a), be dismissed or otherwise removed from office.\n\nA person who has been dismissed or otherwise removed from office for a contravention of the provisions specified in clause\n\nis disqualified from holding any other State office.","clauses":[{"clauseNumber":"(1)","text":"A State officer shall behave, whether in public and official life, in private life, or in association with other persons, in a manner that avoids- (a) any conflict between personal interests and public or official duties; (b) compromising any public or official interest in favour of a personal interest; or (c) demeaning the office the officer holds."},{"clauseNumber":"(2)","text":"A person who contravenes clause (1), or Article 76, 77 or 78(2)- (a) shall be subject to the applicable disciplinary procedure for the relevant office; and (b) may, in accordance with the disciplinary procedure referred to in paragraph (a), be dismissed or otherwise removed from office."},{"clauseNumber":"(3)","text":"A person who has been dismissed or otherwise removed from office for a contravention of the provisions specified in clause"},{"clauseNumber":"(2)","text":"is disqualified from holding any other State office."}],"plainExplanation":"Violating integrity requirements leads to disqualification from holding any public office in Kenya."},{"articleNumber":76,"title":"Financial probity of State officers","content":"A gift or donation to a State officer on a public or official occasion is a gift or donation to the Republic and shall be delivered to the State unless exempted under an Act of Parliament.\n\nA State officer shall not- (a) maintain a bank account outside Kenya except in accordance with an Act of Parliament; or (b) seek or accept a personal loan or benefit in circumstances that compromise the integrity of the State officer.","clauses":[{"clauseNumber":"(1)","text":"A gift or donation to a State officer on a public or official occasion is a gift or donation to the Republic and shall be delivered to the State unless exempted under an Act of Parliament."},{"clauseNumber":"(2)","text":"A State officer shall not- (a) maintain a bank account outside Kenya except in accordance with an Act of Parliament; or (b) seek or accept a personal loan or benefit in circumstances that compromise the integrity of the State officer."}]},{"articleNumber":77,"title":"Restriction on activities of State officers","content":"A full-time State officer shall not participate in any other gainful employment.\n\nAny appointed State officer shall not hold office in a political party.\n\nA retired State officer who is receiving a pension from public funds shall not hold more than two concurrent remunerative positions as chairperson, director or employee of- (a) a company owned or controlled by the State; or (b) a State organ.\n\nA retired State officer shall not receive remuneration from public funds other than as contemplated in clause (3).","clauses":[{"clauseNumber":"(1)","text":"A full-time State officer shall not participate in any other gainful employment."},{"clauseNumber":"(2)","text":"Any appointed State officer shall not hold office in a political party."},{"clauseNumber":"(3)","text":"A retired State officer who is receiving a pension from public funds shall not hold more than two concurrent remunerative positions as chairperson, director or employee of- (a) a company owned or controlled by the State; or (b) a State organ."},{"clauseNumber":"(4)","text":"A retired State officer shall not receive remuneration from public funds other than as contemplated in clause (3)."}]},{"articleNumber":78,"title":"Citizenship and leadership","content":"A person is not eligible for election or appointment to a State office unless the person is a citizen of Kenya.\n\nA State officer or a member of the defence forces shall not hold dual citizenship.\n\nClauses (1) and (2) do not apply to- (a) judges and members of commissions; or (b) any person who has been made a citizen of another country by operation of that country’s law, without ability to opt out.","clauses":[{"clauseNumber":"(1)","text":"A person is not eligible for election or appointment to a State office unless the person is a citizen of Kenya."},{"clauseNumber":"(2)","text":"A State officer or a member of the defence forces shall not hold dual citizenship."},{"clauseNumber":"(3)","text":"Clauses (1) and (2) do not apply to- (a) judges and members of commissions; or (b) any person who has been made a citizen of another country by operation of that country’s law, without ability to opt out."}]},{"articleNumber":79,"title":"Legislation to establish the ethics and anti-corruption","content":"commission Parliament shall enact legislation to establish an independent ethics and anti -corruption commission, which shall be and have the status and powers of a commission under Chapter Fifteen, for purposes of ensuring compliance with, and enforcement of, the provisions of this Chapter."},{"articleNumber":80,"title":"Legislation on leadership","content":"Parliament shall enact legislation- (a) Establishing procedures and mechanisms for the effective administration of this Chapter; (b) prescribing the penalties, in addition to the penalties referred to in Article 75, that may be imposed for a contravention of this Chapter; (c) providing for the application of this Chapter, with the necessary modifications, to public officers; and (d) making any other provision necessary for ensuring the promotion of the principles of leadership and integrity referred to in this Chapter, and the enforcement of this Chapter."}],"chapterNumber":6}]]}],"$L1f"]}]
